 "issue": 2459,
 "issue_title": "Bug: write_parquet accepts non-boolean preserve_attrs values",
 "issue_body": "## Environment / context\n- Repository: im-anishraj/arnio\n- Tested by current `main` source inspection in `arnio/io.py`\n- Published `arnio==1.19.0` does not yet expose `preserve_attrs`; this issue targets the unreleased/current-main API documented on the website\n- Affected area: Parquet export / metadata preservation\n\n## Steps to reproduce\nCurrent `write_parquet()` documents and types `preserve_attrs` as a boolean:\n```python\ndef write_parquet(..., preserve_attrs: bool = True) -> None:\n    ...\n    if df.attrs:\n        if preserve_attrs:\n            ... validate attrs and write metadata ...\n        else:\n            df.attrs = {}\n```\n\nCallers can pass non-boolean values:\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport arnio as ar\n\nsrc = pd.DataFrame({\"x\": [1, 2]})\nsrc.attrs[\"source\"] = \"qa\"\nframe = ar.from_pandas(src)\n\nar.write_parquet(frame, \"out.parquet\", preserve_attrs=\"False\")  # truthy, preserves attrs\nar.write_parquet(frame, \"out.parquet\", preserve_attrs=[])       # falsy, drops attrs\n```\n\n## Expected result\n`preserve_attrs` should reject non-boolean values with a clear `TypeError`, similar to the explicit validation used for `compression` and `row_group_size`.\n\n## Actual result\nThe current implementation relies on Python truthiness. Strings, integers, lists, dictionaries, and other objects can silently change whether metadata is preserved or dropped.\n\n## Severity / impact\nLow-to-medium. This can cause confusing metadata behavior in Parquet exports, especially in notebooks or pipelines where option values may come from parsed config files or environment variables.\n\n## Likely affected area\n- `arnio/io.py::write_parquet`\n- `tests/test_parquet.py`\n- Website/API docs only if the intended accepted type changes\n\n## Suggested next action\nAdd an early guard:\n```python\nif not isinstance(preserve_attrs, bool):\n    raise TypeError(\"preserve_attrs must be a bool\")\n```\nThen add regression tests for `\"False\"`, `0`, `1`, `None`, `[]`, `{}`, and `object()`.\r\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/2459",
 "pr": 2480,
 "pr_title": "Validate write_parquet preserve_attrs type",
 "pr_body": "## Summary\n- Reject non-boolean preserve_attrs values before Parquet export\n- Document the preserve_attrs TypeError contract\n- Add regression coverage for common non-bool inputs\n\nFixes #2459\n\n## Tests\n- uv run --extra dev pytest tests/test_parquet.py -q\n- uv run ruff format --check arnio/io.py tests/test_parquet.py\n- uv run ruff check .\n- uv run pytest -q",
